Corrected the lab's syslog severity map, which ranked syslog `notice` above syslog `warning`, and its message classifier, which filed BGP session-down events as interface-down events.
`invoke start` no longer fails with "network event-tracker-mgmt declared as external, but could not be found": the tasks create the lab's management network when neither compose nor containerlab has, so the stack and the topology can be brought up in either order.
The lab now runs containerlab from its own pinned image rather than expecting it installed, so `invoke lab-up` works on an Apple Silicon Mac - where containerlab cannot be installed at all, needing a Linux kernel - as well as on Linux.
